    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "When run selects stop or observes the incoming channel closed, it calls drainPending and returns. drainPending calls Ack(nil) on each non-nil pending message and ignores acknowledgment errors. Close signals stop and waits for stopped; this drain does not flush pending messages to the handler, iterate buffered incoming messages, or iterate previously delivered in-flight messages. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event/b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914/coalesce.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:9be6cb97aeee49eeae350d25b8c070f8928219c5f68a4475b9d099b93ab7fbe6",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0b95e29f17db583808af08f4767c9157095ed1438f4ab30fef12e98478c5dd30",
            "ev:3b976d804e2b79b14576c13f816c797516d80868804c2de18a36f42802cd8078"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "event-mongodb ca444aedec31e7e959c0932a8f7577c15312f37e; event b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914",
            "recorded_at": "2026-11-02T17:00:00+00:00"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Ordinary output removes the selected entry from pending and marks its key in flight. The ready scan skips in-flight keys until a done signal deletes that marker. Because ready ranges over a map, this implementation does not establish cross-key FIFO delivery; the ordered list serves eviction. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event/b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914/coalesce.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:dac788d42dd150076591c8c8e286af408550cf6713cb8ff55f7a34d81b235d53",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0b95e29f17db583808af08f4767c9157095ed1438f4ab30fef12e98478c5dd30",
            "ev:2253fd5e5bd9bf5e468222b1d61d60a6c0c7a74c2853ef1202bdb62b87a72d77"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "event-mongodb ca444aedec31e7e959c0932a8f7577c15312f37e; event b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914",
            "recorded_at": "2026-11-02T17:00:00+00:00"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "At source level, TestCoalescer_EvictionSkipsInflightKeys waits for queued inputs to be absorbed before releasing the in-flight key, then errors if its pending \"A2\" update is not delivered. TestCoalescer_MaxKeysEviction only logs when the newest \"d\" key is missing; that newest-key check is not a failing assertion. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event/b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914/coalesce_test.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:59380200fa7663afa9988b6478c8eb328445c551967569c1ae16fd4f42ade318",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4fccf93b68295c760adbb12e60eef690b4664d057ebc511f40e0e8e189bf46fd"
          ],
