    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Capacity eviction runs after nonempty-key input handling while the pending map exceeds c.maxKeys. It scans the ordered list for the oldest key that is not in flight, warns, calls entry.msg.Ack(nil), ignores its error, and removes the entry without sending it to output. If every candidate is in flight, the loop stops even while capacity remains exceeded. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event/b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914/coalesce.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c455e28f92f427470533aa6b729397828671ed6051ff75eb2f94161d03effd80",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2253fd5e5bd9bf5e468222b1d61d60a6c0c7a74c2853ef1202bdb62b87a72d77"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "event-mongodb ca444aedec31e7e959c0932a8f7577c15312f37e; event b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914",
            "recorded_at": "2026-11-02T17:00:00+00:00"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Scope inference: this coalescer intentionally removes superseded and capacity-evicted pending events through acknowledgment, and shutdown also acknowledges pending entries. Therefore its source-level contract cannot preserve a complete per-event handler history. The adapter recommends current-state use cases such as cache invalidation and materialized view updates. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event-mongodb/ca444aedec31e7e959c0932a8f7577c15312f37e/coalesce.go",
