    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Metadata coalescing selects in.msg.Metadata()[metaKey] before payload decoding; the raw coalescer stores the message and a superseded count rather than a decoded payload. This avoids decoding messages that are superseded. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event/b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914/coalesce.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:fd06d85f122efd0091af79966087d9530f34eb52e2c8641953534a838a0d6cdc",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4e3eb58eca42ac4d3230711bf2f290e8eff8205a8e42a49bba502f54219dbc7f",
            "ev:684068899ba98413c29b8eb3c73c6fe0877f0310e2c3e943099bd687d6def269"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "event-mongodb ca444aedec31e7e959c0932a8f7577c15312f37e; event b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914",
            "recorded_at": "2026-11-02T17:00:00+00:00"
          },
          "also": [
            "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event/b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914/option.go"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When a nonempty key already has a pending entry, handleInput calls old.msg.Ack(nil), discards the acknowledgment error, replaces the entry with the newer message, increments the superseded count, and moves the key to the back of the eviction list. It supersedes the pending entry rather than the already delivered in-flight event. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event/b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914/coalesce.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e5ca4e6f34596754a201de0fc410860ae350c24abee6a5414d2dd135f601ea67",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0b95e29f17db583808af08f4767c9157095ed1438f4ab30fef12e98478c5dd30",
            "ev:2253fd5e5bd9bf5e468222b1d61d60a6c0c7a74c2853ef1202bdb62b87a72d77",
            "ev:4a7dcdc591270b4e2af53ccc92c1dfb6cc871aa745492af2dcd6bb0f6648622a",
            "ev:684068899ba98413c29b8eb3c73c6fe0877f0310e2c3e943099bd687d6def269"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "event-mongodb ca444aedec31e7e959c0932a8f7577c15312f37e; event b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914",
            "recorded_at": "2026-11-02T17:00:00+00:00"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "For an empty extracted key, handleInput stores the message under \"__nokey__\" plus the message ID and returns before supersession and capacity checking. It makes the message eligible for ordinary output rather than synchronously invoking the handler. The bypass assumes distinct generated keys: reusing a message ID can overwrite a pending entry under that same synthetic key. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event/b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914/coalesce.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:869fdd8ffd8e0fd73f7023f97af116d544f86d8ac6ef04743af7218c128afbb9",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0b95e29f17db583808af08f4767c9157095ed1438f4ab30fef12e98478c5dd30",
            "ev:2253fd5e5bd9bf5e468222b1d61d60a6c0c7a74c2853ef1202bdb62b87a72d77"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "event-mongodb ca444aedec31e7e959c0932a8f7577c15312f37e; event b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914",
            "recorded_at": "2026-11-02T17:00:00+00:00"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The pinned API comment for WithCoalesceMaxKeys says an evicted oldest entry is delivered to the handler. The pinned handleInput implementation instead acknowledges and deletes that entry. This is an attributed documentation-versus-implementation conflict; use the implementation to describe the automatic acknowledgment boundary. (medium confidence)",
