            "recorded_at": "2026-11-02T17:00:00+00:00"
          },
          "also": [
            "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event-mongodb/ca444aedec31e7e959c0932a8f7577c15312f37e/context.go"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "At source level, TestRawCoalescer_SupersedesByMetadataKey first delivers one message, queues two messages under the same metadata key, waits for inputsHandled to advance before signaling done, then asserts that the next message ID is \"3\" and its superseded count is at least one. The counter handshake controls absorption before release; these are fixture assertions, not execution results from this research. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event/b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914/coalesce_test.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b256c1bfe2bba5bff6dd0398ceb1c384bd14e3ac23b7cfd4ed1d631bce8f7c13",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:132c59835412a52ee101156d8b9ecc6a87842f23a22f65a9bb341970920e1416",
            "ev:f1603777d1164b64167c7f7239977d0038393e046313201a9f81c737f6f54202"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "event-mongodb ca444aedec31e7e959c0932a8f7577c15312f37e; event b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914",
            "recorded_at": "2026-11-02T17:00:00+00:00"
          },
          "also": [
            "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event/b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914/coalesce.go"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The empty-key and missing-metadata fixtures assert delivery of their respective messages. TestCoalescer_ShutdownDrainsPending waits for a pending input to be absorbed and fails if Close does not return before its timeout; it does not count acknowledgment callbacks or assert a successful business effect. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event/b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914/coalesce_test.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:07b071ac234197f1fa3345bd11b4043ea5aefcfda63aee39a7675a560f431d1e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:189bfa6fac9afebe3a74b0636ca60f27d42e8273352b858ef4d487e7017843a2",
            "ev:84e3e7c16495261d55847f3891f9b99d5703bf707b2b5cc7082f52499545564b"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "event-mongodb ca444aedec31e7e959c0932a8f7577c15312f37e; event b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914",
            "recorded_at": "2026-11-02T17:00:00+00:00"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The MongoDB adapter fixture uses a channel transport and a blocked-first-handler handshake with five published same-key messages. Its final assertions require fewer than five handler deliveries, a nonzero coalesced count, and delivered-plus-coalesced at least one. They do not require exact accounting of all five, exactly two deliveries, or the identity of the latest payload; this fixture does not exercise a live MongoDB transport. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbaliyan/event-mongodb/ca444aedec31e7e959c0932a8f7577c15312f37e/coalesce_unit_test.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c60fc2b6159ec49e69fcd69e52184da10850bd2981e1a7b697bd84a2e9c8a78b",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1ffc3acc032b6a6aa159e70bbfd2cc142a7610c736ef41309e51884e9a7e303d"
          ],
          "temporal": {
            "applicability_version": "event-mongodb ca444aedec31e7e959c0932a8f7577c15312f37e; event b112463682d44b0e57d8545e3cdf5d51e112e914",
            "recorded_at": "2026-11-02T17:00:00+00:00"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The WithCoalesceByKey documentation explicitly describes coalescing state as ephemeral across restarts. The shared coalescer constructs pending and in-flight maps inside run. Its in-memory coalescing history supplies no durable restart history by itself. (medium confidence)",
